- `<F1-1>` = Fix shape, as the deployment report states it: give the API a transient-retry and connect budget that outlasts a wake (its EF retry policy and connect timeout, the API half of the first-click work that was not kept), or keep the database awake, which removes the wake. Since 11:53 AEDT on 2026-11-01 the UAT database is kept awake (no pause in 21 quiet minutes), so the gap does not arise on UAT; it remains in code for any database that pauses, for example the hosted demo if it pauses. Related: HPSMPOC-426 (the first-click fix) and HPSMPOC-207 (a transient SQL login reset at API start-up). Done when: a database wake no longer loses a read to an API 500 in a measured visit on an environment that pauses, or the item is recorded as declined. Which fix is built is a scope call that is not made here.
